        "Question": "What is the difference between ventilation and air conditioning?",
        "Answer": "Air conditioning cools the indoor air and lowers its humidity, while ventilation replaces stale air with fresh outdoor air and removes odors. An enclosed building needs both for its occupants' comfort and good air quality."
